From 0516b6849db3b99554e457486e544f5a1eda3ea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:34:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - align authenc sources at every message length

Limiting authenc source bouncing to inputs below eight bytes still exposes
intermittent corruption in larger requests. On AN7581 with raw MXBRSTSZ 6
and 64/64 buffer thresholds, SHA224/RFC3686 case 740 corrupts the final
three payload bytes and its four-byte tag. The input has 65 bytes of AAD,
16385 bytes of payload and a source offset of one. The destination already
uses an aligned bounce buffer.

Restore word-aligned sources for all native authenc lengths. Keep the
diagnostic bypass off by default. This is a source-buffer workaround;
the precise cause of the observed DMA corruption is still unconfirmed.

Retain byte-aligned read-only AES skcipher sources, the DES/3DES guard,
the raw-6 burst default and the disabled size-based AES fallback. Cipher
and hash computation still use the accelerator for eligible authenc
requests after the source copy.

Signed-off-by: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 eip93-common.c | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/eip93-common.c b/eip93-common.c
index c34d9cc..b605c33 100644
--- a/eip93-common.c
+++ b/eip93-common.c
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@ static bool eip93_is_sg_aligned(struct scatterlist *sg, u32 len,
 
 		/*
 		 * DMA-written buffers must not share cache lines with CPU writes.
-		 * Read-only sources follow the cipher and short-message policy.
+		 * Read-only sources follow the cipher and authenc alignment policy.
 		 * dma_map_sg() maps the entire entry, including any bytes beyond
 		 * the requested crypt length in the last entry.
 		 */
@@ -319,12 +319,11 @@ static int check_valid_request(struct eip93_cipher_reqctx *rctx)
 	int err = -EINVAL;
 
 	/*
-	 * Allow byte-aligned AES reads, but keep DES/3DES sources aligned.
-	 * Short authenc inputs can span only partial words: require aligned
-	 * sources below two words, using AAD plus payload before adding the tag.
+	 * Allow byte-aligned AES skcipher reads. DES/3DES and authenc need
+	 * aligned sources: unaligned authenc input tails have been corrupted
+	 * for both short and long messages.
 	 */
-	allow_unaligned = IS_AES(rctx->flags) &&
-			  (!authsize || totlen_src >= 2 * sizeof(u32));
+	allow_unaligned = IS_AES(rctx->flags) && !authsize;
 	if (src != dst)
 		allow_unaligned |= authsize ? READ_ONCE(aead_unaligned_src) :
 					     READ_ONCE(skcipher_unaligned_src);
-- 
